.TH MU2E-POWER-STATE 1 "2026-09-18" "mu2edaq-power-recovery 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Operations"
.SH NAME
mu2e-power-state \- phase 1: read-only survey of the Mu2e DAQ clusters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2e-power-state
.RB [ \-\-location
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-node
.IR HOST ]
.RB [ \-\-principal
.IR PRINCIPAL ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs phase 1 of
.BR mu2e-power-recovery (1)
and nothing else: a read-only survey of every node in the selected locations.
It takes no corrective action, so it is safe to run at any time, including
while the DAQ is taking data.
.PP
The survey proceeds in the order an operator actually asks the questions:
.IP 1. 4
Are the gateways up, and can they be logged in to? If no gateway can be reached
the phase stops, because everything else is probed through one.
.IP 2. 4
Do the gateways have their expected mounts, routing and IPMI-segment access?
.IP 3. 4
From a gateway, what answers ICMP, and what does each BMC say about the chassis
it controls?
.IP 4. 4
For everything that answers: disks, mounts, interfaces, link speeds, services,
PCIe cards and kernel state.
.PP
Its results are written to the
.I initial-state.html
report page and to
.IR data/assess.json ,
and are recorded in the run store so that later phases can compare against
them. In particular the BMC event-log length is recorded here, so phase 2 can
report only the events its own power-on produced.
.SH LOGINS
Each node is entered with the operator's own Kerberos principal first \(em
always, and for root sessions as much as for ordinary ones. Only when a host
refuses it are the Mu2e service identities tried, and a service identity that
worked is remembered for that host as a fallback, never ahead of the personal
principal. The login name comes from
.IR ssh.user " and " ssh.root_user ,
not from the principal.
.PP
When
.I ssh.login
fails, the remaining SSH checks for that node are skipped: one refusal is
enough, and twelve more connections would each be refused the same way. A
changed host key is reported as such rather than as a login failure, because no
credential can get past it; see
.B DIAGNOSING A REFUSED LOGIN
in
.BR mu2e-power-recovery (1).
.SH OPTIONS
Every option of
.BR mu2e-power-recovery (1)
is accepted except
.BR \-\-phase ,
which is fixed to
.BR assess .
The reasoning behind each is given there; the list below is what this command
takes and what each does here.
.SS Run control
.TP
.BI \-\-label " TEXT"
Label for this run, shown in the report header and the logbook subject.
.TP
.B \-\-execute
Accepted, and has no effect: this phase changes nothing by construction.
.TP
.B \-\-simulate
Contact nothing at all; answer every command from the built-in script. Use it
to exercise the survey and the report off site.
.TP
.BI \-\-location " NAME"
Limit the survey to one location:
.BR mc2 ", " mc1 " or " teststand .
Repeatable. Defaults to
.IR topology.locations .
.TP
.BI \-\-node " HOST"
Limit the survey to these nodes. Repeatable; short or fully-qualified names are
both accepted.
.TP
.B \-\-continue\-on\-error
Accepted; it governs phase 2 and has no effect here.
.TP
.BI \-\-from " STAGE" ", " \-\-until " STAGE"
Accepted; they bound the phase-2 power-on sequence and have no effect here.
.TP
.B \-\-include\-failed
Accepted; it governs phase 3 and has no effect here.
.SS Credentials
.TP
.BI \-\-principal " PRINCIPAL"
Kerberos principal for ordinary logins. If there is no usable ticket, a
password is prompted for and
.BR kinit (1)
is run into a credential cache private to the run.
.TP
.BI \-\-root\-principal " PRINCIPAL"
Kerberos principal with root access on the nodes. It is kept in a credential
cache separate from the ordinary one. Ten of the twenty-five checks open a root
session:
.IR ssh.login_root ", " login.users ", " disk.smart ", " disk.errors ,
.IR disk.raid ", " net.forwarding ", " svc.nfs_export ", " svc.firewall ,
.IR pcie.devices " and " pcie.driver .
.B \-\-list\-checks
prints all twenty-five.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-prompt
Never prompt for a password; fail with instructions instead. For unattended
runs.
.TP
.BI \-\-vault\-addr " URL"
HashiCorp Vault address, for the BMC credentials the power checks need.
.SS Report
.TP
.BI \-\-output\-dir " DIR"
Where the report pages are written. Default:
.IR html/ .
.TP
.B \-\-publish
Copy the report to
.I report.publish.target
afterwards.
.TP
.BI \-\-publish\-target " DEST"
Override the publication target. Implies
.BR \-\-publish .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-report
Do not write the HTML pages; console output only.
.TP
.B \-\-post\-ecl
Accepted; the logbook entry is written by phase 4. See
.BR mu2e-power-report (1).
.TP
.BI \-\-run\-id " N"
Accepted; only phase 4 reads it. See
.BR mu2e-power-report (1).
.SS General
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the option summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print
.I mu2edaq-power-recovery 0.1.0
and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Main configuration file. Default:
.IR config/power-recovery.yaml .
.TP
.BI \-\-env\-file " FILE"
Dotenv file. Default:
.IR config/.env .
.TP
.BI \-\-database\-url " URL"
SQLAlchemy URL for the run store.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-self\-update
Skip the phase-0 check for a newer revision.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-checks
Print every registered check and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-nodes
Print the node inventory and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the survey as JSON on stdout instead of tables.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Debug logging, including one line per credential attempted against each host.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Warnings and errors only.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every node passed every applicable check.
.TP
.B 1
At least one node failed a check or could not be reached.
.TP
.B 2
The survey could not start, or no gateway could be logged in to.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.EX
mu2e-power-state
mu2e-power-state \-\-location teststand
mu2e-power-state \-\-node mu2e-mgr-01 \-\-node mu2e-dl-01 \-v
mu2e-power-state \-\-json > state.json
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2e-power-recovery (1),
.BR mu2e-power-on (1),
.BR mu2e-ssh-probe (1),
.BR mu2edaq-checks.yaml (5)
